#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Hero-specific counter notes -- a third knowledge layer beyond the
stats-based matchup_matrix.json and the tag-based item_counters.json, on
top of SPEC.md's original scope.

Source: dota2.fandom.com's per-hero "Counters" pages (e.g.
https://dota2.fandom.com/wiki/Spirit_Breaker/Counters), fetched via
Fandom's MediaWiki API (api.php?action=parse&prop=wikitext) -- the regular
page URLs are blocked by a Cloudflare bot-challenge, but this API endpoint
isn't. Every note below is a paraphrase in my own words, not copied wiki
text; item mentions are pulled from the specific hero-pair's writeup, not
the page's general item section.

Batch 1 (ordered by hero id): Anti-Mage, Axe, Bane, Bloodseeker,
Crystal Maiden, Drow Ranger, Earthshaker, Juggernaut, Mirana, Morphling,
Shadow Fiend, Phantom Lancer, Puck, Pudge, Spirit Breaker.

Batch 2 (ids 15-30): Razor, Sand King, Storm Spirit, Sven, Tiny,
Vengeful Spirit, Windranger, Zeus, Kunkka, Lina, Lion, Shadow Shaman,
Slardar, Tidehunter, Witch Doctor.

Batch 3 (ids 31-45): Lich, Riki, Enigma, Tinker, Sniper, Necrophos,
Warlock, Beastmaster, Queen of Pain, Venomancer, Faceless Void,
Wraith King, Death Prophet, Phantom Assassin, Pugna. Enigma and Phantom
Assassin have unusually deep wiki pages (30+ pairs each); everything else
follows the same per-pair-with-real-mechanics rule as batches 1-2.

Batch 4 (ids 46-60): Templar Assassin, Viper, Luna, Dragon Knight,
Dazzle, Clockwerk, Leshrac, Nature's Prophet, Lifestealer, Dark Seer,
Clinkz, Omniknight, Enchantress, Huskar, Night Stalker. Luna and Viper
have unusually deep wiki pages; pure ally-synergy lines ("X makes a
powerful ally for Luna") were skipped since they aren't counter
interactions.

Batch 5 (ids 61-76, skipping 71 done in batch 1): Broodmother, Bounty
Hunter, Weaver, Jakiro, Batrider, Chen, Spectre, Ancient Apparition,
Doom, Ursa, Gyrocopter, Alchemist, Invoker, Silencer, Outworld
Destroyer (Outworld Devourer's page redirects here). Alchemist's own
page also redirects, to Bloodchemist/Counters. Chen and Jakiro have
unusually deep wiki pages.

Batch 6 (ids 77-91, skipping 85/86 covered here too since they
naturally fell in this run): Lycan, Brewmaster, Chaos Knight,
Disruptor, Io, Keeper of the Light, Lone Druid, Meepo, Naga Siren,
Nyx Assassin, Ogre Magi, Rubick, Shadow Demon, Treant Protector,
Undying. Rubick and Naga Siren have unusually deep wiki pages; Rubick's
page is mostly "what to steal" commentary, so only entries with a real
mechanical interaction (interrupts, dispels, item counters) made the
cut rather than every generic "steal this spell" line.

Batch 7 (ids 92-106): Visage, Slark, Medusa, Troll Warlord, Centaur
Warrunner, Magnus, Timbersaw, Bristleback, Tusk, Skywrath Mage,
Abaddon, Elder Titan, Legion Commander, Techies, Ember Spirit. Four of
these (Centaur Warrunner, Bristleback, Abaddon, Legion Commander)
redirect to oddly-named alternate pages on the wiki (Centaur
Bloodrunner, Bristleblood, Bloodaddon, Blood Commander) -- verified
the wikitext is genuinely about the real hero (real ability names)
before using it, so this is just a wiki page-naming quirk, not a
different hero or a hoax page.

Batch 8 (ids 107-114, 119-121, 123, 126, 128 -- the newer-hero-id
range skips gaps for heroes not yet released at spec time): Earth
Spirit, Underlord, Terrorblade, Phoenix, Oracle, Winter Wyvern, Arc
Warden, Monkey King, Dark Willow, Pangolier, Grimstroke, Hoodwink,
Void Spirit, Snapfire. Terrorblade has an unusually deep wiki page.

Batch 9 (final batch, ids 129-155): Mars, Dawnbreaker, Marci,
Primal Beast, Muerta -- this covers every hero with a wiki Counters
page as of this writing. Ring Master, Kez, and Largo have NO
/Counters page on dota2.fandom.com at all (confirmed via the API's
"missingtitle" error, not a fetch failure) -- they're simply too new
or nobody's written one yet, so they have no entry in
HERO_COUNTERS and won't appear in hero_specific_counters.json until
someone writes their wiki page; the app already handles heroes
missing from this file gracefully (no hero-specific notes, nothing
else affected). Primal Beast's own page has old leftover vandalism
(a dead "#REDIRECT [[Pudge/Counters]]" line plus an unrelated
Wikipedia link, both inert -- the API's returned title confirms it
is NOT an active redirect) sitting inside the "Bad against..."
section which also broke that section's top-level heading, so the
automated extractor's section-splitter silently dropped that whole
section; the content was recovered by reading the raw wikitext
directly instead. If re-running the pipeline picks up a cleaned-up
version of that page later, it's fine to leave this hand-curated
entry as is or refresh it — the merge behavior means it won't be
touched either way.

Each hero's list mixes both directions from its wiki page: entries where
the enemy counters this hero, and entries where this hero counters the
enemy. Direction isn't a separate field -- the note text itself makes it
clear which way the advantage runs. Coverage is the wiki's individually-
explained hero pairs; the page's grouped "heroes who buy Linken's" /
"durable heroes" -style lists without individual reasoning were left out
to keep every entry backed by real explained mechanics, not just a shared
category label -- worth revisiting if useful.

Re-run after editing HERO_COUNTERS below; safe to run multiple times.
"""
